' Body of deployment.puml / deployment-dark.puml. No start marker, so PlantUML
' will not render this file directly, and naming one in a comment here breaks
' the include. See README.md.
'
' Every colour is a wrapper variable so the dark render is dark throughout.
' Both post-render passes in README.md are required for either half.

' Widened into a fallback stack by a post-render pass, see README.md.
skinparam defaultFontName Inter

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title Deployment: one image, four exposure problems

header
<b>One image.</b>  The entrypoint takes a service name: Kubernetes runs <b>args: ["text"]</b>, compose runs <b>command: text</b>.
endheader

actor "legacy Mumble\nclient" as legacy $c_neutral
actor "Fancy client" as fancy $c_blue

package "cluster" as K8S $c_faint {

  node "**Service: LoadBalancer**\n**TCP** 64738" as lbtcp $c_red
  node "**Service: LoadBalancer**\n**UDP** 64738\nsessionAffinity: **none**" as lbudp $c_red
  node "**Ingress**\nHTTPS" as ing $c_green2

  node "**gateway** pods\nreplicas: N\nstateful per connection,\n**resumable elsewhere**" as gwpod $c_gw
  node "**session store**\nsequence + replay buffer\n**«not built»**: in-process,\ndies with the pod" as sstore $c_gw2
  node "**voice** pods\nreplicas: N\nholds ciphers + membership cache" as vpod $c_core
  node "**files/http** pods\nstateless" as fpod $c_green
  node "**essential** pods\nsession · permissions\nmetadata · userdata" as epod $c_ess
  node "**optional** pods\npush · audit · social · ..." as opod $c_green
  node "**directory**\nsingleton per server instance\nno inbound port" as dpod $c_indigo
}

cloud "**publist.mumble.info**" as publist $c_indigo
dpod -[$l_indigo]-> publist : hourly HTTPS
note right of dpod $c_indigo
  No `Service`, no `Ingress`, no port: outbound only.
  **replicas: 1** is a correctness bound, not a capacity one.
  Each replica announces on its own timer, so two replicas
  are two registrations of the same server.
end note

legacy --> lbtcp
fancy  --> lbtcp
lbtcp  --> gwpod

legacy --> lbudp
fancy  --> lbudp
lbudp  --> vpod

fancy --> ing
ing   --> fpod

gwpod -[$l_blue]-> epod : gRPC + circuit breaker
gwpod -[$l_blue]-> opod : gRPC
gwpod -[$l_blue]-> vpod : gRPC\n(signalling + UDPTunnel only)
gwpod -[$l_blue]-> sstore : sequence + replay
vpod  -[$l_blue].-> epod : membership snapshot

note right of lbtcp $c_red
  **1. The gateway cannot use an Ingress.**
  `Ingress` is HTTP/HTTPS only; Mumble is raw TCP+TLS.
  Needs `Service type=LoadBalancer` or Gateway API `TCPRoute`.
end note

note right of lbudp $c_red
  **2. Client affinity is the wrong affinity.**
  Audio routes per channel, so a channel's members must share a
  pod. `sessionAffinity: ClientIP` pins each *client*, scattering
  a channel across pods, and there is **no inter-pod audio path**.
  Discord assigns a *channel* to a voice server and tells the
  client which. Mumble has no such field, and **a legacy client**
  **sends UDP to the port it made TCP to**, so it cannot be
  redirected. In order of increasing capability:
  · one voice pod per server instance, vertical only
  · a forwarding mesh between pods, costs a hop
  · shard by channel + an explicit endpoint in `ServerSync` for
    Fancy clients; legacy stays on the advertised pod
  See scaling.puml.
end note

note bottom of vpod $c_core
  **3. A restarted voice pod has cold caches.**
  Ciphers and the membership cache do not survive, and audio
  arriving before it re-subscribes is dropped.
  `/readyz` gates on **cache warm-up**, not on the process being
  alive, and must be a *different* endpoint from `/healthz`.
end note

note right of sstore $c_gw2
  **4. RESUME, or a rolling deploy is a DDoS.**
  Draining a pod holding 10 000 clients means 10 000 full floods
  of every ChannelState and UserState at once. A sequence number
  replays only the gap, but it must **outlive the pod**, or a
  client landing elsewhere has nothing to resume against.
  Legacy clients cannot resume: stagger readiness and send a
  jittered reconnect hint.
end note

note bottom of ing $c_green2
  files/http is the only component speaking HTTP, so it is the
  only one that gets TLS termination and a CDN for free.
end note

note as COMPOSE $c_card
  **docker compose**: the same picture with the load balancers
  replaced by published ports. **Twenty-one containers** from one
  image, started in tier order, differing only in `command`.
  voice publishes UDP 64738 and the gateway TCP 64738, so a
  legacy client still sees one host:port pair.
  **--all-in-one** collapses every pod into one process.
  **«not built»: no in-process pipes.** A service resolves its own
  endpoint through the broker, which cannot know it before it has
  registered, so every service falls back to its local socket.
end note
